==Trivia==
*The "Pirate King" in this sub-chapter's name is someone who pirates movies, as each stage references a popular movie or movie series.
**[[Stylist Mononoke]] references ''[[:wikipedia:Princess Mononoke|Princess Mononoke]]''.
**[[Stand By Motel]] references ''[[:wikipedia:Stand by Me (film)|Stand by Me]].
**[[Aven-Jazz Cafe]] references ''[[:wikipedia:The Avengers (2012 film)|The Avengers]]''.
**Both the English and Japanese names of [[Retreat of the Living Dead]] reference the film ''[[:wikipedia:The Return of the Living Dead|The Return of the Living Dead]].'' The name of the stage in the Japanese Version is pronounced similarly to ''Battalion'', the Japanese name of ''The Return of the Living Dead''. Through this, it can also be assumed that its name in the English Version is meant to reference the film's original English title.
**[[Titanic Steakhouse]] references ''[[:wikipedia:Titanic (1997 film)|Titanic]]''.
**[[Inn-Dependence Day]] references ''[[:wikipedia:Independence Day (1996 film)|Independence Day]]''. The presence of [[Johnnyleon]], an [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]], may reference the alien invasion in the movie.
*Bazaar of the Pirate King is the only [[Uncanny Legends]] sub-chapter to have a new map image.

